{"step_index":9253,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T04:38:54Z","thinking":"Creating a Bash script to enforce immutability on specific files and directories, drawing the list from a protected registry and including critical system configuration files. Considering the dependencies: the immutability script's functionality necessitates the prior removal of elevated privileges, as `chattr +i` would otherwise be bypassable. The immutability script's list will be expanded to encompass vital configuration files to further secure the system.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"#!/usr/bin/env bash\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# /home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/03-immutable-files.sh (DRAFT ONLY)\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# Purpose: Applies Linux Inode Immutability (chattr +i) to critical configurations\\n#          and architecture specifications.\\n#\\n# ARCHITECTURAL SECURITY COUPLING (WHY THIS WORKS):\\n# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n# In the previous audit, 'chattr +i' was classified as \\\"bypassable\\\" because:\\n#   AGY -> child process -> sudo -> root -> chattr -i <file>\\n#\\n# Once Step 1 (01-sudoers-restricted.draft) is active:\\n# 1. 'chattr' is STRICTLY EXCLUDED from sudoers (deny-by-default).\\n# 2. 'azureuser' has CapEff = 0 (zero Linux capabilities).\\n# 3. Removing '+i' requires the kernel capability CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE.\\n# 4. Without sudo access to chattr and without CAP_LINUX_IMMUTABLE, AGY cannot\\n#    remove '+i' under ANY circumstances (even via C, Python, or direct syscalls).\\n# 5. Direct syscalls (SYS_unlink, SYS_rename, SYS_truncate) will return:\\n#    errno 1: EPERM (Operation not permitted) directly from the ext4 filesystem.\\n# ==============================================================================\\n\\nset -euo pipefail\\n\\necho \\\"=== [DRAFT EXECUTION] APPLYING EXT4 INODE IMMUTABILITY ===\\\"\\n\\n# List of critical architecture files to protect\\nPROTECTED_FILES=(\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/AGENTS.md\\\"\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/PROJECT_REGISTRY.md\\\"\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/safety_levels.json\\\"\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/POLICIES/protected_registry.json\\\"\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/.gemini/config/hooks.json\\\"\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/.bashrc\\\"\\n    \\\"/home/azureuser/.profile\\\"\\n)\\n\\nfor file in \\\"${PROTECTED_FILES[@]}\\\"; do\\n    if [[ -f \\\"$file\\\" ]]; then\\n        echo \\\"[+] Setting immutable flag (+i) on: $file\\\"\\n        # Command must be run as root by Iraq Bhai during harde\n<truncated 653 bytes>","Description":"\"Draft script to apply ext4 immutability (+i) and explanation of sudoers coupling\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/03-immutable-files.sh\"","toolAction":"\"Drafting immutability script\"","toolSummary":"\"Draft 03-immutable-files.sh\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
