{"step_index":9255,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T04:38:59Z","thinking":"Step four involves setting up an external, immutable backup using a WORM (Write Once Read Many) policy in Azure Blob Storage. This requires the use of command-line tools for configuration. A crucial constraint is that the configuration *must* be executed from outside the virtual machine to ensure proper immutability.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# EXTERNAL IMMUTABLE BACKUP ARCHITECTURE (WORM & REMOTE GIT)\\n\\nTarget Host: Azure VM `FatehAli`\\nStatus: DRAFT SPECIFICATION (NO ACTIONS EXECUTED)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. WHY EXTERNAL IMMUTABLE BACKUP IS MANDATORY\\n\\nEven with strict sudoers and `chattr +i`, an attacker or kernel failure could corrupt local disks.\\nThe ONLY truly impenetrable defense against total VM compromise is **Storage Outside the VM**:\\n- The VM possesses **ZERO Azure credentials** and **NO Managed Identity**.\\n- Therefore, data stored in an Azure Blob Storage container with **Immutable Blob Storage (WORM - Write Once, Read Many)** cannot be deleted or overwritten by ANY process inside the VM.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. AZURE BLOB WORM POLICY SETUP (EXECUTE FROM AZURE CLOUD SHELL)\\n\\n> 🛑 **CRITICAL OPERATIONAL REQUIREMENT:**\\n> These Azure CLI commands **CANNOT** and **MUST NOT** be executed from inside the `FatehAli` VM.\\n> They must be executed by Iraq Bhai from **Azure Cloud Shell** (https://shell.azure.com) or an external admin workstation.\\n\\n### Step 1: Create a Dedicated Backup Storage Account\\n```bash\\n# Set your target Azure variables\\nRESOURCE_GROUP=\\\"fatehali-rg\\\"\\nLOCATION=\\\"eastus\\\" # Or your VM region\\nSTORAGE_ACCOUNT=\\\"fatehalibackupstorage$RANDOM\\\"\\nCONTAINER_NAME=\\\"immutable-vm-backups\\\"\\n\\n# Create standard general-purpose v2 storage account\\naz storage account create \\\\\\n    --name \\\"$STORAGE_ACCOUNT\\\" \\\\\\n    --resource-group \\\"$RESOURCE_GROUP\\\" \\\\\\n    --location \\\"$LOCATION\\\" \\\\\\n    --sku Standard_LRS \\\\\\n    --kind StorageV2 \\\\\\n    --allow-blob-public-access false\\n\\n# Create container\\naz storage container create \\\\\\n    --name \\\"$CONTAINER_NAME\\\" \\\\\\n    --account-name \\\"$STORAGE_ACCOUNT\\\" \\\\\\n    --auth-mode login\\n```\\n\\n### Step 2: Configure Time-Based WORM Immutability Policy\\n```bash\\n# Create an immutability policy (e.g. 30 days retention where NO ONE can delete or overwrite)\\n# Set policy mode to Unlocked first to test, then Locked for permanent WORM protection\\naz storage container immutability-policy create \\\\\\n    --a\n<truncated 1966 bytes>","Description":"\"External immutable backup architecture guide with Azure CLI WORM commands and Git sync script\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/home/azureuser/AGY-MASTER/DRAFTS/04-external-backup-setup.md\"","toolAction":"\"Drafting external backup architecture\"","toolSummary":"\"Draft 04-external-backup-setup\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
